     `StoplossGuard` considers all trades with the results `"stop_loss"`, `"stoploss_on_exchange"` and `"trailing_stop_loss"` if the resulting profit was negative.
     `trade_limit` and `lookback_period` will need to be tuned for your strategy.
 
+#### Consecutive Losses Guard
+
+`ConsecutiveLossesGuard` looks at the most recently closed trades (for one pair, or across all pairs) and counts how many of them, starting from the latest, lost money in a row. A single trade that closed with a profit above `required_profit` breaks the streak and resets the count.
+
+Unlike `StoplossGuard` and `LowProfitPairs`, this protection does not use `lookback_period` - it only cares about the *order* trades closed in, not how long ago they closed.
+
+Once `trade_limit` losing trades have happened back-to-back, trading will stop for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+This applies across all pairs, unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, which will then only look at one pair at a time - locking only the pair that had the losing streak, and allowing other pairs to keep trading.
+
+For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a series of long losses.
+
+`required_profit` will determine the required relative profit for a trade to break the streak. This should normally not be set and defaults to 0.0 - which means any losing trade counts towards the streak.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair for 12 candles after 3 losing trades in a row on that pair.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "ConsecutiveLossesGuard",
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": True,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
+To instead pause the whole bot after 5 consecutive losses across all pairs, set `only_per_pair` to `False` (the default):
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "ConsecutiveLossesGuard",
+            "trade_limit": 5,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 24,
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 #### MaxDrawdown
 
 The `MaxDrawdown` protection evaluates trades that closed within the current `lookback_period` (or `lookback_period_candles`).  
